      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T20:56:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This block is forced to use `Optional\u003cLong\u003e` all throughout the block and on the `throttleRetryPolling()` because of the condition of being executed only when `e.isRetry() \u003d\u003d true`.\n\nUsing `Optional\u003cLong\u003e` as a parameter is an anti-pattern in Java and makes the code much less readable.\n\nThe whole block makes sense only when `e.isRetry() \u003d\u003d true`; why not simply use a traditional and more readable `if()` statement instead?\n\n\n\n```suggestion\n      T id, E e, IndexEntityChecker\u003cT, E\u003e entityChecker) {\n    if (e.isRetry()) {\n      long millisSinceAttempt \u003d millisSinceLastAttempt(e);\n      if (!throttleRetryPolling(millisSinceAttempt)) {\n        return IndexingResult.FAILURE;\n      }\n\n      if (millisSinceAttempt \u003c retryInterval) {\n        return IndexingResult.THROTTLED;\n      }\n    }\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 74,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 83,
        "endChar": 5
